# REQUIRES: unsanitized-code
# copied() becomes part of the loop that calls it. There the read of `from[k]` has no test in front of it: it asks by itself whether `k` lies below the length, and answers undefined.
# It is told the length that `k < from.length` compares with, which is read in front of both loops. So the two ask the same and one of them goes, no length is read or written
# in the loop that pushes, and its turns can be counted ahead of it, so it needs no poll.
